---
// "Beyond the tiers": the sixteen Reception stations, with the notes that
// say what on them is ours rather than the catalogue's. Reception-only.
// The content is src/data/packages/reception-stations.ts; the browsing
// behaviour is reception-package.js (see StationsBrowser for the two
// layouts).
import StationsBrowser from "./StationsBrowser.astro"
import "./ReceptionStations.css"
---

<section
  class="section-padding package-stations package-stations-hybrid on-dark on-dark-gold-wash"
  id="stations-hybrid"
  aria-labelledby="stations-hybrid-title"
>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <div class="eyebrow" data-reveal>
        Beyond the tiers
      </div>
      <h2 id="stations-hybrid-title" data-reveal style="--d: 80ms">
        Stations your guests will <em>remember</em>
      </h2>
      <p class="lead" data-reveal style="--d: 160ms; margin-top: 22px">
        Sixteen tables and towers to layer onto any{" "}
        <a href="#reception-tiers" class="link-underline-inline">
          Reception tier
        </a>{" "}
        — Daisy, Lavender or Rose — each priced per person and carved, shucked or built to
        order.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="package-stations-hybrid-mobtab">
      <StationsBrowser variant="stage" />
    </div>

    <div class="package-stations-hybrid-desktop">
      <StationsBrowser variant="carousel" />
    </div>

    <div class="package-stations-photo-note" data-reveal>
      <svg
        width="16"
        height="16"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.6"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="M12 9v4m0 4h.01M10.3 3.9 2.5 17.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 3.8 20h16.4a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.3-2.5L13.7 3.9a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-2.6 0Z" />
      </svg>
      <span>
        Station photography above is illustrative placeholder imagery, not of Bacchus — to
        be replaced with the venue's own.
      </span>
    </div>
    {/* Sits alongside the photography note and carries the same
         oxblood treatment for the same reason: it is the only thing
         on the page telling a reader that these badges are inferred
         rather than given. DO NOT DELETE while that is true. The
         catalogue marks (V) across the Reception tiers but not once
         across the Stations list, so unlike the Reception tier menus above
         — where every badge is the client's own — all thirty-six
         here are our reading of a dish name. Same reasoning that
         kept high-tea-package.html unmarked entirely; the difference
         is that this page shows the guesses and says so, rather than
         withholding them. */}
    <div class="package-stations-photo-note package-stations-veg-note" data-reveal>
      <svg
        width="16"
        height="16"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.6"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="M12 9v4m0 4h.01M10.3 3.9 2.5 17.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 3.8 20h16.4a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.3-2.5L13.7 3.9a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-2.6 0Z" />
      </svg>
      <span>
        <span class="package-veg-marker" aria-hidden="true">
          V
        </span>{" "}
        marks a dish we believe to be vegetarian. Unlike the Reception tier menus, the
        catalogue gives no vegetarian markings for the stations, so every mark here is
        inferred from the dish name and none is confirmed by Bacchus. Three things in
        particular need checking before this is shown to a guest: cheeses, which depend on
        whether animal or microbial rennet is used — Parmigiano Reggiano, Camembert, Blue
        Stilton and Ġbejna are left unmarked for that reason, and the cheeses that are
        marked are assumptions; stocks and sauces in the pasta, risotto and stir-fried
        dishes; and the marshmallows on the Crêpe Table, left unmarked as gelatine is
        usual. Dressings served on oysters and lobster are not marked at all, as the dish
        beneath them is not vegetarian.
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="package-stations-photo-note package-stations-labels-note" data-reveal>
      <svg
        width="16"
        height="16"
        viewBox="0 0 24 24"
        fill="none"
        stroke="currentColor"
        stroke-width="1.6"
        stroke-linecap="round"
        stroke-linejoin="round"
        aria-hidden="true"
      >
        <path d="M12 9v4m0 4h.01M10.3 3.9 2.5 17.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 0 3.8 20h16.4a1.5 1.5 0 0 0 1.3-2.5L13.7 3.9a1.5 1.5 0 0 0-2.6 0Z" />
      </svg>
      <span>
        The six groupings above — Boards &amp; Cured, Fruits of the Sea, Grill &amp;
        Roast, Across Asia, Pasta &amp; Pizza, To Finish — are our own editorial grouping,
        not the catalogue's or Bacchus's. The catalogue lists all sixteen stations flat,
        and this grouping also reorders them away from catalogue order.
      </span>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
